        "Content": "Very attractive period home in one of Dublin's most sought after coastal locations.\r\n\r\nThis 5-star Dublin rental has so much to offer discerning clients; the property has been lovingly upgraded and embellished throughout the years but still retains all the charm and characteristics synonymous of the Georgian era.\r\n\r\nOffering elegant living, captivating sea views, off street parking and superb gardens - early viewing advised.\r\n\r\nLocation Dun Laoghaire\r\n\r\nTivoli Terrace is within strolling distance of the promenade and a multitude of shopping facilities at Dun Laoghaire Town Centre as well as the IMC Cinema, Pavilion Theatre, Lexicon Library, bars and many restaurants. Public \r\n\r\nTransport via the 46A bus and DART makes commuting to and from the city centre very simple.\r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\n\r\nReception Hall (8m x 1.8m)with ornate cornicing, centre rose, ornate balustrade with a monkey tail, Phonewatch alarm system, understairs storage and door to Guest W.C. \r\n\r\nDrawing Room (4.7m x 6.4m)\r\n\r\nwith original fireplace and surround with brass effect, ornate ceiling coving and centre rose, refurbished sash windows with panoramic sea views and double doors onto the raised deck area\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room (4.6m x 6.5m)\r\n\r\nwith open fire with marble effect surround, built in book shelving, refurbished sash windows with panoramic sea views, double doors to the raised decking, if fitted with an Andrew Ryan kitchen comprising wall and floor units, centre island unit, built in fridge/freezer, integrated dishwasher, Siemens four ring gas hob, extractor fan, Siemens oven and Siemens microwave\r\n\r\nHalf Landing \r\nwith picture arched window overlooking the rear and door to\r\n\r\nUtility Room \r\nwith tiled floor and plumbed for washing machine & dryer\r\n\r\nFirst Floor Landing \r\nwith access to the attic and recessed lighting\r\n\r\nMaster Bedroom (4.6m x 4.3m)\r\nwith built in wardrobe, window to rear and door to En Suite Bathroom (1.9m x 3.9m)\r\nwith bath, heated towel rail, separate shower, w.c., wash hand basin, ornate fireplace, part tiled walls, sash windows with shutters and with sea views\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (4.6m x 3m)\r\nwith ornate fireplace, double sash windows with shutters intact and sea views\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (3m x 4.5m)\r\nwith double glazed windows overlooking the rear\r\nFamily Shower Room with fully tiled walls and floor, shower, w.c., wash hand basin, heated towel rail, sash window with shutters intact and sea views\r\n\r\nOutside \r\nthe south facing garden to rear has two raised decked areas, a patio area, flower beds, mature plants, shrubbery and trees, two separate patio areas and a large shed\r\nRequest Viewing\r\nShow Number\r\nProperty Features\r\nFrom: €5,495 monthly\r\n Period Residence by the sea\r\n Stunning sea views and gardens\r\n Strolling distance to promenade\r\n All mdern luxuries\r\n Close to all amenities\r\n Easy access to dublin city\r\nFive Star Magazine\r\nOUR TOP STORIES\r\nWe're off to Sunny Spain!\r\n\r\nWe're off to Sunny Spain! \r\nDirect Investment into Spain reached 52 Billion € in 2018 - the highest level ever! ...\r\nRead more"
